{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "features": [
    {
      "id": "modern4e.feature.wizard-spellbook",
      "title": "Spellbook",
      "description": "You possess a spellbook, a book full of mystic lore in which you store your rituals and your daily and utility spells.",
      "access": {
        "type": "always"
      },
      "prerequisites": {
        "type": "always"
      },
      "selection": {
        "maximum": 1,
        "constraints": []
      },
      "coverage": {
        "status": "UNIMPLEMENTED",
        "limitations": [
          "Shared local authoring definition; runtime interpretation and combat effects remain unimplemented.",
          "Power acquisition through level 10 and daily/utility preparation capacities are structured. Technique choices remain unresolved until the magic-technique catalog is adapted; no arbitrary technique becomes eligible. Page costs, levels 11-30 acquisitions and extended-rest execution remain incomplete."
        ]
      },
      "sections": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You possess a spellbook, a book full of mystic lore in which you store your rituals and your daily and utility spells."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "title": "Daily and Utility Powers"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Your spellbook holds your wizard daily attack powers and wizard utility powers (not including your cantrips). You begin with four daily attack powers in your spellbook, two of which you can prepare on any given day. Each time you gain a level that lets you select a wizard daily attack power or a wizard utility power, choose two different powers of that type at that level and add them to your book. After each extended rest, you can prepare a number of daily attack powers and utility powers according to what you can use per day for your level (see the Wizard Powers Prepared per Day table). You can't prepare the same power twice on the same day.\n\nIf you replace a power because of gaining a level or through retraining, the previous power vanishes from your spellbook and is replaced by the new power."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "title": "Techniques"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Your book also contains three 1st-level magic Techniques of your choice that you have mastered. At 5th level, and again at 11th, 15th, 21st, and 25th level, you master two more Techniques of your choice and add them to your spellbook. When you choose the Techniques , they must be your level or lower."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "title": "Capacity"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A typical spellbook has 128 pages. Each power takes up 1 page. A Techniques takes up a number of pages equal to its level."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "title": "Wizard powers prepared per day",
          "columns": [
            "Level",
            "Daily",
            "Utility"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "1",
              "2",
              "-"
            ],
